= BITwiki computational scope review =

This register makes existing questions visible under [[BITwiki:Computational scope]]. It does not treat a valid source citation, a formal model, the ability to digitize measurements or an unrelated <code>Related to</code> edge as proof that a concept belongs in BITwiki.

'''This page tracks 36 scope candidates: 27 delegated first-pass decisions and nine identities (five clusters) with conditional owner acceptance of the proposed computational/applied-science direction, but no finalized replacement titles.''' These are editorial triage outcomes, not completed rewrites, migrations or factual-validity verdicts. An existing Core page stays in place until any contextualization or redirect operation is separately reviewed against links and depth variants. K01 remains <code>UNVERIFIED</code> until a purpose rationale is independently reviewed. Preserve source and revision lineage.

