== Next implementation contract ==

'''Do not simply rename the nine articles using the example labels above.''' First examine scholarly/technical usage for each potential subject name and decide whether it denotes a recognized field, an independently reusable computational method, or an application/case study. Prepare an evidence-based choice showing whether the existing page's scientific content can remain as context and whether another page already covers the same conceptual identity.

For each proposed mapping, audit:
# Current Core title and existing Simple/Technical presentations;
# incoming and outgoing wikilinks and typed semantic links; 
# intended canonical name, precise mechanism/method, scientific terminology evidence and missing review material;
# page text to preserve, reframe or relocate, with provenance and uncertainty;
# redirects and deployment/preflight consequences;
# source code and staging validation, plus separately authorized live deployment.

'''The immediate next batch is scholarly terminology and identity verification, not bulk content expansion or automatic migration.''' Ask the owner only when two source-grounded choices remain meaningful. Existing pages remain in source-controlled staging unchanged until a reviewed migration is separately authorized.

== Review record ==

For each page, record the editorial outcome, computational mechanism or method, relevant observing/measuring evidence, whether independent identity is needed, and whether linked Simple/Technical variants and semantic edges require reconciliation. Update the record as each page is actually reviewed. The 27 delegated decisions above express a provisional canonical treatment, not a completed K01 claim review or an executed redirect. The nine canonical-title decisions remain unresolved despite agreement on the general direction; the owner should receive evidence-based alternatives and dependency impact before choosing. Each subsequent article change must record its evidence, reader-depth impact and graph-link dependencies; update the outcome only after a concrete review.

== Release boundary ==

GitHub <code>main</code> is the integrated source; staging compilation and CI cannot approve K01, publish changes to the live MediaWiki or remove existing site pages. Re-scope should proceed through bounded, reviewed changes with explicit dependency and redirect considerations when renaming or contextualizing a canonical page.

